 "captions": [
  [
   0.0,
   4.019,
   "Part six. The graph variant, Mem0g. Flat facts"
  ],
  [
   4.019,
   7.535,
   "can't express how things relate. Graphs can."
  ],
  [
   8.035,
   11.627,
   "Mem0g stores memory as a directed, labeled graph."
  ],
  [
   12.259,
   15.851,
   "Nodes are entities: people, places, objects, events, each"
  ],
  [
   15.851,
   19.443,
   "with a type, an embedding, and a creation"
  ],
  [
   19.443,
   19.892,
   "time."
  ],
  [
   20.523,
   24.115,
   "Edges are relationships, stored as triplets: source, relation,"
  ],
  [
   24.115,
   27.707,
   "destination. Riya, lives in, Pune. Riya, loves, cricket."
  ],
  [
   28.339,
   31.931,
   "Extraction happens in two LLM stages. An entity"
  ],
  [
   31.931,
   35.523,
   "extractor finds the entities and their types. Then"
  ],
  [
   35.523,
   39.114,
   "a relationship generator decides which pairs are connected,"
  ],
  [
   39.114,
   40.91,
   "and labels the edge."
  ],
  [
   41.542,
   45.134,
   "When Riya moves to Bengaluru, a conflict detector"
  ],
  [
   45.134,
   47.828,
   "notices the old lives in edge."
  ],
  [
   48.46,
   52.051,
   "It isn't deleted. It's marked invalid. So the"
  ],
  [
   52.051,
   55.643,
   "graph still knows where she used to live,"
  ],
  [
   55.643,
   58.786,
   "which is exactly what temporal questions need."
  ],
  [
   59.286,
   62.03,
   "Integrating a new triplet is careful work."
  ],
  [
   62.662,
   65.798,
   "Mem0g embeds the source and destination entities, and"
  ],
  [
   65.798,
   68.933,
   "searches for existing nodes whose similarity is above"
  ],
  [
   68.933,
   70.109,
   "a threshold t."
  ],
  [
   70.741,
   73.877,
   "If a node already exists, it's reused. If"
  ],
  [
   73.877,
   77.013,
   "not, a new node is created. That can"
  ],
  [
   77.013,
   79.756,
   "mean zero, one, or two new nodes."
  ],
  [
   80.388,
   83.132,
   "Then the edge is added, with metadata."
  ],
  [
   83.763,
   86.899,
   "This is entity resolution: Bengaluru and Bangalore should"
  ],
  [
   86.899,
   89.643,
   "end up as one node, not two."
  ],
  [
   90.143,
   92.613,
   "Retrieval uses two strategies at once."
  ],
  [
   93.245,
   96.538,
   "Entity-centric search finds the entities mentioned in the"
  ],
  [
   96.538,
   99.831,
   "question, matches them to nodes, and walks their"
  ],
  [
   99.831,
   103.124,
   "incoming and outgoing edges to build a small"
  ],
  [
   103.124,
   103.536,
   "subgraph."
  ],
  [
   104.168,
   107.461,
   "Semantic triplet search embeds the whole question, scores"
  ],
  [
   107.461,
   110.754,
   "it against a text encoding of every triplet,"
  ],
  [
   110.754,
   113.636,
